WEBVTT

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:15.640
My right hand holds a bowl of gold,

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.180
And my left holds one of silver.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.720
Never one without the other,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:37.800
Two unseen bowls for each of us.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:46.210
The golden one is filled with joy,

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:53.550
shining warmly.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.350
Since we met, my golden bowl

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:05.360
cannot hold all my happiness and love.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:15.500
Golden joy, silver sadness,

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:22.850
I would leave my past behind...

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:27.580
For you, for the sake of love,

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:34.520
I would empty the bowls of my past.

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.860
I wonder whether you should know the reason why...

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:10.530
The surgery, you see. They had to remove one.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.560
Five years... When a relapse occurs within five years... there isn't really any hope...

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:22.200
That's why we broke up.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.350
That's why I left the man I loved.

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:29.170
I don't know whether I have a long life left before me or not...

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:32.050
I don't want to be a burden in my loved one's life.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:37.920
I felt that, because I loved him, I had no choice but to let him go.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.270
I feel that it was for the best.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:47.950
I don't regret it at all...

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.750
I'm sorry...

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:55.900
I see that I should never have told you all of that...

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.990
Still... it's strange, isn't it?

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:04.740
You aren't related by blood, but...

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:07.090
...the two of you seem alike, somehow.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:08.230
What...?

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:13.250
I felt like I could talk to you about this because you're Takehiko-san's little sister.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:18.470
S... sister?

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:20.610
Little sister? You mean...?!

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.630
You didn't know...!!

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.310
I- I'm sorry!

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:27.980
I'm...

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:31.600
You mean... I'm really my brother's little sister...?!

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:37.570
<b>37. Merry-Go-Round</b>

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.580
<i>I'm sorry! I'm so sorry...</i>

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:59.480
<i>You were writing letters to him and all, so I just thought that you must have known...</i>

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:03.430
<i>I didn't know! I didn't know about it at all!</i>

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:05.580
<i>Well you see, Takehiko-san...</i>

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:19.180
Papa... Mama...

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:23.770
What?

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:25.980
She's a bit late, don't you think?

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:28.650
Yes...

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.190
Hmm...

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:31.940
Shall I pour you some fresh tea?

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:35.890
No... I think I'm going to take a little walk.

00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:37.970
Down to the station?

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:39.710
Ah... er, no...

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:45.070
Goodness, dear. Don't worry about her. I'll call Tomoko-san in a little bit.

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:48.020
Ah... OK. Could you, please?

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:50.790
She'll be just fine.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.870
Yes... Yes, OK.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:56.480
Earlier...

00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:00.590
...I received a call from Takehiko.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:03.610
It seems he's decided to study abroad in Germany.

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:05.280
Germany?

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.750
Has he, now...

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:10.290
I wonder if he's leaving it up to me...

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:12.360
Maybe the time has finally come.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:16.990
I think it's about time for Nanako to learn about everything.

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:20.710
If that's what you feel is best, dear.

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:27.830
<i>My dear brother...</i>

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:31.180
<i>...I didn't know what to do...</i>

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:33.830
<i>I felt so mixed up inside...</i>

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:35.900
<i>Saint-Juste-sama's death...</i>

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:41.320
<i>Kaoru-no-Kimi's love - and the scars, both physical and emotional...</i>

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:44.970
<i>And on top of that, there is the matter between the two of us...</i>

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:47.720
<i>It's like the whole world has turned upside down on me.</i>

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:49.930
<i>I... I...</i>

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:57.960
Nanako, may I come in?

00:05:58.560 --> 00:05:59.900
Nanako?

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:00.970
I'm coming in.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:18.830
<i>Takehiko-san is Professor Misonoo's son by his previous wife.</i>

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:28.800
Dear...?

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:34.370
No... I think that Nanako might be hurt to learn of it now.

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:37.710
She's such a kindhearted girl...

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:42.330
If she were to learn that I abandoned Takehiko and his mother, she would really be hurt.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:45.700
You didn't <i>abandon</i> them...

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:49.720
Regardless of the circumstances, that's what it amounts to in the end.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.460
Dear...

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:54.340
Or maybe I just don't have the courage to do it.

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:59.020
Maybe I'm just afraid that Nanako will hate me for it.

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:00.770
I'll talk to her.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:02.980
No... no, that won't do.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.630
Papa! Good morning!

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:25.500
Hey there. 'Morning.

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:26.980
I'll go get in the paper.

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:27.920
Ah, OK...

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:33.550
<i>At any rate... at any rate, I've decided to ask him.</i>

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:38.300
<i>I'll ask Papa about the truth; I figure that I'll have time to think over it more after that.</i>

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:42.970
Papa...

00:07:42.970 --> 00:07:46.390
Want to go for a walk, Nanako?

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:47.460
Eh?

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:48.660
Uh, sure...

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:05.410
It was right here...

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:08.630
This was the place, Nanako. Do you remember?

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:13.670
Yes... yes, I remember.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:17.170
This is where you and I first met, Nanako.

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.970
The place where Papa and I first met...

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:28.880
The first time you saw me, you looked like you were afraid of me.

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:32.630
Well, you were just standing there looking at me like that.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:35.380
You didn't even say hello.

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:37.920
But... well...

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:40.940
From that point on, you were my daughter.

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:43.950
My one and only daughter...

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:52.960
My dear, precious Nanako... your Papa has only ever once told you a lie...

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:57.910
Or rather, there was something I never told you, which amounts to the same thing.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:03.570
The truth is... I have a son.

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:08.530
I had a child with the woman I was with before I married your mother.

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:14.020
He's about seven years older than you. He is your step-brother.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:19.840
I'll be honest with you, though...

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:22.720
...even though it's been thirteen years since I saw him last...

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:27.340
...I love my son every bit as much as I love you.

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:36.500
He is in my thoughts always, just as you are.

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:44.110
I'm so sorry, Nanako.

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:49.800
Aside from this one thing, I truly feel that I've been the Papa that you always considered me to be.

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:55.150
Nanako...

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:58.730
Do you want to see him again, Papa?

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:01.210
Henmi Takehiko-san...

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:02.280
Nanako!

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:05.650
I'm happy! I'm so happy!

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:09.600
Papa, if... if you had said that you didn't love my brother...

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:12.010
...if you had turned out to be that sort of person...

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:14.020
...I don't know what I would have done!

00:10:14.950 --> 00:10:16.160
Nanako!

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:18.290
Papa!

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:20.630
Papa... Papa...

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:26.160
Nanako...

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:31.030
<i>My dear brother...</i>

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:34.580
<i>...it was so sunny in the morning, but it turned rainy in the afternoon.</i>

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:37.260
<i>Even so, I went out.</i>

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:40.340
<i>I went out; I just couldn't stay put.</i>

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:44.790
<i>I wanted to see you, no matter what.</i>

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.470
<i>I just had to.</i>

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:57.350
Coming!

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:02.470
Hey.

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:05.680
Er... what happened? You're totally soaked.

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:09.000
That day, when it snowed!

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:10.070
Eh?

00:11:10.070 --> 00:11:12.350
I said it that day, when it was snowing!

00:11:14.550 --> 00:11:16.160
That snowy day...

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:22.070
The last class day of the cram school course...

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:24.680
<i>OK everyone, you have five minutes to work this problem.</i>

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:25.020
<i>Ahh!!</i>

00:11:27.710 --> 00:11:30.790
You had been teaching us.

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:33.550
It was our last day together.

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:40.440
I had made up my mind to say it.

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:42.710
I knew it was silly; I was really nervous.

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:47.470
<i>Have a question? OK. Which page?</i>

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:50.890
<i>P... pl- please...</i>

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:52.900
<i>Please be my big brother!</i>

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:01.450
Not a lover, or even a friend...

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:05.060
...just... I thought... if you would just read my letters...

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:06.870
Yes, that's right.

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:08.680
I remember it well.

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:10.890
May I say it one more time?

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:11.430
Eh?

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:14.510
Please be my big brother!

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:16.580
Because... you really are my brother!

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:32.690
That was so mean of you, really!

00:12:32.690 --> 00:12:36.840
Papa told me, you know. "Takehiko knew all along that you were his little sister."

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:39.670
That wasn't very nice of you, really.

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:41.720
Sorry.

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:44.190
I did intend to tell you, eventually.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.340
When? Well, when?

00:12:46.340 --> 00:12:49.150
Er... well, ah...

00:12:49.150 --> 00:12:51.230
So cruel of you, really...

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:53.440
That's why I said I'm sorry.

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:57.130
If... if I hadn't ever found out...

00:12:57.130 --> 00:13:00.610
...if I had just continued writing to you like this, then eventually...

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:03.960
...eventually... the letters alone wouldn't have been enough...

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:07.910
If... if I'd really fallen in love with you...

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:11.260
...what would you have done about it, then?

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:12.070
Eh?

00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:16.020
I haven't ever actually dated a boy yet, but...

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:20.040
...if I were to do so, I imagine that he'd find me to be the <i>persistent</i> type.

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:25.430
But... I knew from the start that you were my younger sister, so...

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:28.250
We're not related by blood, though.

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:30.860
So, if I'd started feeling that way, it wouldn't have mattered.

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:32.800
Ah... er... but...

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:38.830
What? Oh, come on!

00:13:41.030 --> 00:13:43.040
You really had me going there...

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:55.800
It's raining again.

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:56.540
Raining...?

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:59.650
Yes... Once again, it is raining...

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:03.200
Every day that's important to me somehow, it ends up raining.

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:04.740
It seems that way, anyway.

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:07.530
The rain, eh...?

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:10.260
Come to think of it, it was raining on that day, too...

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:11.670
Eh?

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:14.800
Ah... nothing...

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:18.890
<i>It was raining that day, too...</i>

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:25.340
<i>I was hoping to catch a glimpse of my father, who had left me and my mother to remarry.</i>

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:27.750
<i>I was standing there, in the rain...</i>

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:31.950
<i>And then, I saw you for the first time.</i>

00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:33.960
<i>You looked so very precious...</i>

00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:39.070
<i>Who are you?</i>

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:42.280
<i>Who are you?</i>

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:50.040
<i>You had dirt all over your hands, and you were holding a little red shovel.</i>

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:52.650
<i>You gazed at me with those lovely eyes as you spoke...</i>

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:55.430
Who are you?

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.750
<i>That was it, no more than five minutes...</i>

00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:03.680
<i>Bye-bye! Come see me again!</i>

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:07.900
<i>Come see me again!</i>

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:11.590
<i>That faraway day... that rainy day...</i>

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:15.210
<i>You may have forgotten, but I remember.</i>

00:15:15.210 --> 00:15:17.150
<i>Misonoo Nanako...</i>

00:15:17.150 --> 00:15:20.230
<i>From that day forward... I had a little sister.</i>

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:25.030
Who are you? Who are you?

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:30.910
"Nanako..."

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:31.780
Eh?

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:35.200
Ah... no... could I call you "Nanako-kun" from now on?

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:42.430
I'd be happiest if you called me "Nanako".

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:45.720
OK.

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:55.100
<i>My dear brother...</i>

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:59.720
<i>...you really were my brother. Henmi Takehiko-sama.</i>

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:04.380
<i>A really, truly wonderful brother...</i>

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:06.390
<i>Longed after by Fukiko-sama...</i>

00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:08.870
<i>Loved by Kaoru-no-Kimi...</i>

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:14.690
<i>Those enchanting, dark brown eyes, sparkling now just as they did in that day so long ago...</i>

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:19.440
<i>My dear brother... I'm glad that I am your sister.</i>

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:21.850
<i>I think that it's a good thing, really.</i>

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:25.950
<i>After all, no matter how wonderful you may be...</i>

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:29.160
<i>...as my brother, you could never really love me in a romantic way... unfortunately...</i>

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:33.180
<i>I'll keep writing letters to you, the same as before.</i>

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:37.810
<i>No, I'll do my best to write even more, as many and as often as I can!</i>

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:41.290
<i>And then, sooner or later...</i>

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:44.580
<i>...sooner or later, I'm sure, we'll run across one another again.</i>

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:49.060
<i>I don't know where yet, but I'll see those dark brown eyes of yours again someday...</i>

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:50.070
<i>Heh heh heh!</i>

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:56.680
<i>I've been able to write it all down, through happiness and heartache...</i>

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:59.890
<i>...through confusion and uncertainty, all my bittersweet trials...</i>

00:16:59.890 --> 00:17:04.110
<i>...everything, in my own way...</i>

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:07.870
<i>P.S. Of course, I can't send you</i> this <i>letter.</i>

00:17:08.530 --> 00:17:10.540
<i>Nope, I won't do it!</i>

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.960
Yeah, Henmi here...

00:17:25.340 --> 00:17:26.610
Hello?

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:32.810
It's you, isn't it.

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:34.350
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:17:34.350 --> 00:17:36.090
No trouble. What's up?

00:17:36.090 --> 00:17:40.110
<i>I only called because I have something that I need to apologize to you about.</i>

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:44.870
Well, I have quite a few things that I'd like to talk to you about.

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:51.800
I thought that she knew, and so inadvertently told Misonoo-san that she is your younger sister.

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:54.750
I'm sorry; I did something that I shouldn't have.

00:17:55.150 --> 00:17:56.350
<i>Kaoru - </i>

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:18.200
I want to see you...

00:18:22.920 --> 00:18:24.460
I want to see you...

00:18:25.730 --> 00:18:29.020
Rei... I want to see him...

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:31.030
Rei... Rei!

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:41.040
<i>The carousel!</i>

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:42.650
<i>Let's ride the carousel again!</i>

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:55.820
<i>Can you see it?</i>

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:57.370
<i>What?</i>

00:18:57.370 --> 00:18:58.710
<i>I can!</i>

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:01.660
<i>I can see it!</i>

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:06.010
<i>Out beyond the carousel...</i>

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:09.710
<i>...out past the spinning sky-planes...</i>

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:13.720
<i>...I can see it. I see it!</i>

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:19.750
<i>What is it? What can you see?</i>

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:22.230
<i>My future! Everything from here on...</i>

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:25.470
<i>With one turn. I see myself tomorrow...</i>

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:28.410
<i>The second time around, I see myself the day after that!</i>

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:30.810
<i>On the third pass...</i>

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:33.490
<i>Well then...</i>

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:35.360
<i>...this "future you," what's she like?</i>

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:38.110
<i>She loves Takehiko-san even more tomorrow than she does today!</i>

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:42.030
<i>The day after that, she loves you even more!</i>

00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:46.490
<i>With each passing day, she loves you even more than the day before!</i>

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:49.230
<i>All right, then!</i>

00:19:49.240 --> 00:19:51.980
<i>I'd better stop that carousel before we get carried away!</i>

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:54.980
<i>You'll never get it to stop! Never!</i>

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:56.390
<i>Sounds like I'm in trouble, then!</i>

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:20.920
But now, Rei...

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:23.600
...no matter how many times the carousel goes around...

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:27.360
...I don't see anything on the other side.

00:20:48.590 --> 00:20:52.340
Professor, the gentleman with the appointment is here to see you.

00:20:52.340 --> 00:20:54.350
Show him in.

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:55.420
Yes, sir.

00:20:56.840 --> 00:20:58.580
Please, come in.

00:20:58.580 --> 00:21:00.260
Thank you.

00:21:10.440 --> 00:21:14.730
I know you must be busy today; thank you for having the time to see me.

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:25.100
So you've have decided to study at the University of Schellenberg.

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:26.370
Yes, sir.

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:29.650
You need a letter of recommendation and a guarantor's voucher, I suppose?

00:21:29.650 --> 00:21:32.800
Yes, if you would be so kind, sir.

00:21:33.530 --> 00:21:34.940
I understand.

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:37.490
I'll get them to you as soon as possible.

00:21:37.490 --> 00:21:39.160
Will that be all right?

00:21:39.160 --> 00:21:41.640
Yes, sir. Thank you very much.

00:21:42.760 --> 00:21:43.760
Sure.

00:21:56.200 --> 00:21:57.280
Sir...

00:21:57.280 --> 00:21:58.080
Ah!

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:00.020
If that will be all, then...

00:22:00.020 --> 00:22:02.440
Ah... yes, OK...

00:22:03.090 --> 00:22:05.900
Truly, thank you so very much, sir.

00:22:05.900 --> 00:22:06.910
No, it's all right...

00:22:08.230 --> 00:22:10.240
Sorry to have bothered you.

00:22:17.630 --> 00:22:18.900
To the station...

00:22:20.960 --> 00:22:23.240
Shall we walk together as far as the station?

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:24.240
Sure!

00:22:24.240 --> 00:22:26.850
OK! Well, let's get going, then.

00:22:49.560 --> 00:22:51.900
So, what's it up to now, anyway?

00:22:51.900 --> 00:22:53.110
Sir?

00:22:53.110 --> 00:22:54.780
Your height.

00:22:54.780 --> 00:22:56.790
185 cm.

00:22:56.790 --> 00:22:58.000
Is it, now...

00:22:59.890 --> 00:23:01.230
Yes, sir.

00:23:02.570 --> 00:23:06.050
Yes... you've grown so much in the thirteen years since I last saw you...

00:23:09.760 --> 00:23:13.520
Well... I have to go off that way now, so...

00:23:13.520 --> 00:23:14.520
OK.

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:16.430
Goodbye.

00:23:21.580 --> 00:23:22.920
Takehiko!

00:23:26.850 --> 00:23:28.390
Do your best!

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:33.440
Do your best!

00:23:35.030 --> 00:23:37.510
Yes, Father!

00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:14.360
I dreamed I was chasing a rainbow...

00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:19.830
Then the rainbow I was chasing was you.

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:25.440
Before, I had no strength, no will.

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:30.910
But now because of you, I do.

00:24:31.650 --> 00:24:37.190
Feelings of love, like raindrops

00:24:37.190 --> 00:24:42.660
Come pouring from the sky.

00:24:42.660 --> 00:24:45.390
This is surely a game

00:24:45.390 --> 00:24:48.200
Of some mischievous fairy...

00:24:48.200 --> 00:24:50.600
Always dancing,

00:24:50.600 --> 00:24:55.870
Always capricious...

00:25:01.680 --> 00:25:04.430
In the next episode...

00:25:04.430 --> 00:25:10.320
Kaoru continues to obstinately refuse Henmi's love, thinking only of his future.

00:25:11.450 --> 00:25:20.230
Fukiko tries to convince Kaoru that Saint-Juste wanted her to keep thinking of living - to live her life to the fullest.

00:25:21.120 --> 00:25:23.530
Next time: <i>Yes</i>

00:25:23.530 --> 00:25:27.950
<i>My dear brother... there is no end to my tears...</i>
